0..75 Comment "//! The two searches of `boot-core` over `Ptr.Eff`: the first position of a"
76..142 Comment "//! byte in a range, and the first position of a range in a range."
143..146 Comment "//!"
147..221 Comment "//! `find_byte` and `find_range` give the answers of the Rust functions of"
222..299 Comment "//! `crates/boot-core/src/search.rs`. They name no model of memory: the scope"
300..374 Comment "//! that handles `Ptr.Eff` chooses one. Each reads one byte at a time with"
375..452 Comment "//! `load8`, and it reads no byte outside its ranges. An empty range can have"
453..493 Comment "//! any address, and no search reads it."
494..497 Comment "//!"
498..576 Comment "//! Each search descends on the length of its range, as `ranges.gandr` states."
577..580 Comment "//!"
581..659 Comment "//! The `runs` items run the cases of `crates/boot-core/tests/search.rs` under"
660..738 Comment "//! `Extent`. Each range ends at the end of the extent, so a read past it ends"
739..811 Comment "//! the run with `Outside`, as a read past a page with no access faults."
812..815 Comment "//!"
816..875 Comment "//! - see: `ranges.gandr` — `Range`, `Length` and `Found`"
876..950 Comment "//! - see: `../../../library/std/src/ptr.gandr` — `Ptr.Eff` and `Extent`"
951..1026 Comment "//! - see: `../../../crates/boot-core/src/search.rs` — the Rust functions"
